{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\ndef main():\n    rounds = int(input())\n    alice = list(map(int, input().split()))\n    bob = list(map(int, input().split()))\n    \n    bob = bob[1:] + [bob[0]]\n    min_victory, max_victory = 0, 0\n    \n    for idx in range(rounds):\n        max_victory += min(alice[idx], bob[idx])\n    \n    top_bob = max(bob)\n    for idx in range(rounds):\n        if bob[idx] == top_bob and bob[idx] + alice[idx] > min_victory:\n            min_victory = bob[idx] + alice[idx]\n    \n    top_alice = max(alice)\n    for idx in range(rounds):\n        if alice[idx] == top_alice and alice[idx] + bob[idx] > min_victory:\n            min_victory = alice[idx] + bob[idx]\n    \n    min_victory = max(0, min_victory - rounds)\n    print(f'{min_victory} {max_victory}')\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int rounds;\n    cin >> rounds;\n    \n    vector<int> alice(rounds);\n    vector<int> bob(rounds);\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < rounds; i++) {\n        cin >> alice[i];\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < rounds; i++) {\n        cin >> bob[i];\n    }\n    \n    // Rotate bob array: move first element to the end\n    int first = bob[0];\n    for (int i = 0; i < rounds - 1; i++) {\n        bob[i] = bob[i + 1];\n    }\n    bob[rounds - 1] = first;\n    \n    int min_victory = 0, max_victory = 0;\n    \n    // Calculate max_victory\n    for (int idx = 0; idx < rounds; idx++) {\n        max_victory += min(alice[idx], bob[idx]);\n    }\n    \n    // Find top_bob and update min_victory\n    int top_bob = *max_element(bob.begin(), bob.end());\n    for (int idx = 0; idx < rounds; idx++) {\n        if (bob[idx] == top_bob && bob[idx] + alice[idx] > min_victory) {\n            min_victory = bob[idx] + alice[idx];\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Find top_alice and update min_victory\n    int top_alice = *max_element(alice.begin(), alice.end());\n    for (int idx = 0; idx < rounds; idx++) {\n        if (alice[idx] == top_alice && alice[idx] + bob[idx] > min_victory) {\n            min_victory = alice[idx] + bob[idx];\n        }\n    }\n    \n    min_victory = max(0, min_victory - rounds);\n    cout << min_victory << \" \" << max_victory << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.915183232398704e-05, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.2874520507466514e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.145764938177308e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -7.986990567587782e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.0146166207268834e-05, -0.12692877650260925, -0.1427312046289444, -3.576272320060525e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0013273486401885748, -2.145764938177308e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e